# Negative fixture (NESTED position): `lhs ?? rhs` on a non-Option/Result LHS
# must be REJECTED even when the `??` is nested inside another expression shape
# that the (former, incomplete) walk pass did not recurse into. Here the `??` is
# the operand of a unary negation (`EUnaryOp`) — the v1 self-host reject lived on
# the closure-finding `walk_expr_closures` pass, which `else: pass`ed EUnaryOp,
# so this `??` ESCAPED and the self-host silently miscompiled it while Rust
# rejected it (a one-sided reject that failed the Core #8 reference-grade bar).
#
# The reject is now driven from the EXHAUSTIVE `check_carrier_ops_expr` walker
# (typecheck.gg), which visits EVERY sub-expression position, so a `??` nested in
# EUnaryOp / EIndex / EArrayLiteral / EAs / … can no longer escape. Both
# compilers must REJECT this. (AGENTS.md Core invariant #8 — reference-grade,
# reject UB in BOTH backends; #4 — fix the class, not the instance.)
void main():
    int a = 3
    int x = -(a ?? 5)
    print(x)
